      "text": "The given expression consists of a sequence of positive and negative integers. To find the value of the expression, we can group the terms based on their sign. Let's break down the expression into pairs, including a separate term between two pairs: $1 + (-4) + 7 + (-10)$...\n\nTo begin with, let's find the sum of each pair:\n\n$$ 1 + (-4) = -3$$\n$$7+ (-10) = -3$$\n\nSo far, we have:\n\n$$-3 + 1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - 16 + 19 - 22 + 25 - 28 + 31 - 34 + 37 - 40 + 43 - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55 $$\n\nNow let's group the terms with a positive and negative sign together:\n\n$$ (-3 + 1) - (4 + 7) + (13 + (-16)) - (22 + 31) + (37 + (-40)) - (43 + 55) $$\n\nCalculating the sums within each grouping:\n\n$$ -3 + 1 = -2 $$\n\n$$ 4 + 7 = 11 $$\n\n$$ 13 + (-16) = -3 $$\n\n$$ 22 + 31 = 53 $$\n\n$$ 37 + (-40) = -3 $$\n\n$$ 43 + 55 = 98 $$\n\nNow we'll add the individual sums:\n\n$$ -2 - 11 - 3 + 53 - 3 + 98 $$\n\nPerforming these calculations step by step:\n\n$$ -2 - 11 + 53$$\n$$= -13 + 53 $$\n\n$$= 39 $$\n\nFinally, adding one more term:\n\n$$ 39 + (-46) = -7 $$\n\nThus, the value of the given expression is (-7).",
